# Scoped to the memory store so nothing here affects the rest of the repo.
#
# memories.sql is the committed source of truth for every memory, and it is raw UTF-8 -- a
# dump escapes control characters via unistr() but emits ordinary non-ASCII literally (138
# em-dashes and several arrows in this store, measured 2026-08-20). This repo has
# core.autocrlf=true and no other .gitattributes, so git would auto-detect the file as text
# and rewrite its line endings on checkout. `-text` disables that conversion while keeping
# the file diffable in review, which is the entire reason the text export is what we commit.
memories.sql -text diff

# Same reasoning for the generated index: UTF-8 prose, no reason to let git rewrite it.
MEMORY.md -text diff

# The PowerShell scripts are ASCII and CRLF-safe either way, but pinning them keeps a
# checkout byte-identical across machines -- relevant because these are compared by hash
# against the reference project at c:\Projects\ai\memory to spot drift.
*.ps1 -text diff
